WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.757
Spark can inspect a file and try to infer the schema.

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:09.422
That is convenient when we are exploring data, but inference is still a guess.

00:00:09.422 --> 00:00:13.632
A column that looks numeric may actually be an identifier.

00:00:13.632 --> 00:00:16.977
A date may be interpreted as plain text.

00:00:16.977 --> 00:00:21.582
A mostly empty column may be assigned an unexpected type.

00:00:21.582 --> 00:00:26.597
For important pipelines, an explicit schema is often safer.

00:00:26.597 --> 00:00:33.052
It documents what each column is expected to contain and reduces the chance that the same file is interpreted

00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:34.482
differently later.
